e the Democrat around 35%, supporting a modest Republican edge.", "watch": "New independent polling or further disclosure controversies around Herrera could shift this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Texas's 23rd District is an open seat after Tony Gonzales resigned, and Brandon Herrera emerged from a contentious Republican primary against significant outside opposition spending. The district's R+7 lean and a favorable Republican environment give the GOP the edge, and most expert raters call the race Likely Republican, though several rate it a Tossup.\n\nDemocrat Katy Padilla Stout has less money but a professional profile and local press attention, and Herrera's financial disclosure troubles have drawn negative coverage. Prediction markets put the Democrat's chances around a third. The race is competitive but tilts Republican, with meaningful uncertainty given the thin polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3283, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.203, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2999, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3496, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2679, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3125, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3009, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2961, "margin": -4.0}]}